Chapter: UnitRealCompare

 Ordering comparisons on a `unit` type wrapping a `Real`.

 A unit type is erased at codegen, so a comparison has to dispatch on what
 is inside the wrapper. `emit-ord-comparison` matched `RealTy` directly,
 and a `unit Real` resolves to `UnitTy(RealTy)`, which matched neither
 floating arm and fell through to the integer comparator. That is the same
 defect the four scalar ordering operators carried until 2026-07-27, one
 type wrapper deeper, on a path nothing in the tree exercised: no test
 declared a unit over a Real, and the compiler declares none itself.

 It never shipped a wrong answer. `cdx-int-compare-on-float`, added the
 same day the scalar defect was fixed, refused the emit and halted the
 build. The guard was written for a future operator that forgot to
 dispatch; what it actually caught was a future TYPE that did.

 The negative-negative pairs are the ones that matter. Comparing two
 IEEE-754 bit patterns as signed integers is right for two non-negatives
 and right for mixed signs, and reverses for two negatives, so a test that
 only compared positive quantities would pass against the broken emitter.

Section: Units

  Metre = unit Real

  Hertz = unit Real

Section: Operands

  m-neg-big : Metre
  m-neg-big = Metre (0.0 - 2.9)

  m-neg-small : Metre
  m-neg-small = Metre (0.0 - 1.5)

  m-zero : Metre
  m-zero = Metre 0.0

  m-pos-small : Metre
  m-pos-small = Metre 1.5

  m-pos-big : Metre
  m-pos-big = Metre 2.9

  h-lo : Hertz
  h-lo = Hertz 0.0016

  h-hi : Hertz
  h-hi = Hertz 0.0045

Section: The Two Paths

 Asked twice, because a comparison in condition position is fused into the
 branch and one whose result is handed on as a value is materialised. The
 two fused guards already unwrapped the unit and declined it correctly, so
 only the value path was wrong; asking both is what shows that.

  b2i : Boolean -> Integer
  b2i (b) = if b then 1 else 0

  mf-lt : Metre, Metre -> Integer
  mf-lt (a) (b) = if a < b then 1 else 0

  mv-lt : Metre, Metre -> Integer
  mv-lt (a) (b) = b2i (a < b)

  mf-gt : Metre, Metre -> Integer
  mf-gt (a) (b) = if a > b then 1 else 0

  mv-gt : Metre, Metre -> Integer
  mv-gt (a) (b) = b2i (a > b)

  mf-le : Metre, Metre -> Integer
  mf-le (a) (b) = if a <= b then 1 else 0

  mv-le : Metre, Metre -> Integer
  mv-le (a) (b) = b2i (a <= b)

  mf-ge : Metre, Metre -> Integer
  mf-ge (a) (b) = if a >= b then 1 else 0

  mv-ge : Metre, Metre -> Integer
  mv-ge (a) (b) = b2i (a >= b)

  hv-lt : Hertz, Hertz -> Integer
  hv-lt (a) (b) = b2i (a < b)

Section: Report

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
    print-line-uni ("neg-big lt neg-small want 11 got " & show (mf-lt m-neg-big m-neg-small) & show (mv-lt m-neg-big m-neg-small))
    print-line-uni ("neg-big gt neg-small want 00 got " & show (mf-gt m-neg-big m-neg-small) & show (mv-gt m-neg-big m-neg-small))
    print-line-uni ("neg-big le neg-small want 11 got " & show (mf-le m-neg-big m-neg-small) & show (mv-le m-neg-big m-neg-small))
    print-line-uni ("neg-big ge neg-small want 00 got " & show (mf-ge m-neg-big m-neg-small) & show (mv-ge m-neg-big m-neg-small))
    print-line-uni ("neg-small lt neg-big want 00 got " & show (mf-lt m-neg-small m-neg-big) & show (mv-lt m-neg-small m-neg-big))
    print-line-uni ("neg-small gt neg-big want 11 got " & show (mf-gt m-neg-small m-neg-big) & show (mv-gt m-neg-small m-neg-big))
    print-line-uni ("neg-big lt neg-big want 00 got " & show (mf-lt m-neg-big m-neg-big) & show (mv-lt m-neg-big m-neg-big))
    print-line-uni ("neg-big le neg-big want 11 got " & show (mf-le m-neg-big m-neg-big) & show (mv-le m-neg-big m-neg-big))
    print-line-uni ("neg-big ge neg-big want 11 got " & show (mf-ge m-neg-big m-neg-big) & show (mv-ge m-neg-big m-neg-big))
    print-line-uni ("pos-small lt pos-big want 11 got " & show (mf-lt m-pos-small m-pos-big) & show (mv-lt m-pos-small m-pos-big))
    print-line-uni ("pos-big lt pos-small want 00 got " & show (mf-lt m-pos-big m-pos-small) & show (mv-lt m-pos-big m-pos-small))
    print-line-uni ("neg-big lt pos-small want 11 got " & show (mf-lt m-neg-big m-pos-small) & show (mv-lt m-neg-big m-pos-small))
    print-line-uni ("pos-big lt neg-small want 00 got " & show (mf-lt m-pos-big m-neg-small) & show (mv-lt m-pos-big m-neg-small))
    print-line-uni ("neg-small lt zero want 11 got " & show (mf-lt m-neg-small m-zero) & show (mv-lt m-neg-small m-zero))
    print-line-uni ("neg-small gt zero want 00 got " & show (mf-gt m-neg-small m-zero) & show (mv-gt m-neg-small m-zero))
    print-line-uni ("hertz lo lt hi want 1 got " & show (hv-lt h-lo h-hi))
    print-line-uni ("hertz hi lt lo want 0 got " & show (hv-lt h-hi h-lo))
  end
